{
  "slug": "indian-consumer-drafting",
  "name": "Indian Consumer Drafting",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "For every consumer counsel and medical-negligence advocate practising before India's three-tier Consumer Disputes Redressal Commissions — District Commission for claims up to ₹1 crore, State Commission for claims of ₹1 crore to ₹10 crore, and the National Consumer Disputes Redressal Commission for claims above ₹10 crore — this open-source Claude Code plugin standardises drafting under the Consumer Protection Act 2019. Case-config-aware: the parties' Commission tier, pecuniary and territorial jurisdiction, deficiency-of-service / defect-in-goods / unfair-trade-practice / product-liability character, medical-negligence anchor (Jacob Mathew, Martin F. D'Souza, Kusum Sharma, the Bolam standard), Section 69 limitation anchor, and accompanying-application set are user-supplied. Battle-tested for District Section 35 Complaints, State Section 47 originals, NCDRC Section 58 originals, Medical Negligence Complaints, Product Liability Actions under Sections 82-87, Unfair Trade Practice Complaints, Appeals under Sections 41 and 51, Revisional Applications under Section 67, and Execution under Sections 71-72. Six-agent drafting pipeline + shared consumer drafting base with the Consumer Protection Act 2019, CDRC Rules 2020, E-Commerce Rules 2020, Sale of Goods Act 1930, Indian Medical Council (Professional Conduct) Regulations 2002, New Drugs and Clinical Trials Rules 2019, Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita 2023, and Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam 2023 encoded. The finished product is a Commission-ready complaint or appeal the chamber can sign and file across the counter the same day.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **12 skills** and **6 agents**.\n\n- **Skills** (12): `_consumer_drafting_base` (Universal Indian consumer-pleading skeleton), `_drafting_common` (Shared reference for all 10 consumer / medical-negligence / product-liability / unfair-trade-practice / consumer-appeal drafting skills), `consumer-appeal-section-41-district-to-state-draft` (Draft a First Appeal from the District Consumer Disputes Redressal Commission to the State Consumer Disputes Redressal Commission…), `consumer-appeal-section-51-state-to-ncdrc-draft` (Draft a First Appeal from the State Consumer Disputes Redressal Commission to the National Consumer Disputes Redressal Commission…), `consumer-execution-application-section-71-draft` (Draft an Execution Application before the Consumer Disputes Redressal Commission (the Commission that passed the order) under Section…), `consumer-revisional-application-section-67-draft` (Draft a Revisional Application before the National Consumer Disputes Redressal Commission (NCDRC) under Section 67 of the Consumer…), `district-commission-complaint-section-35-draft` (Draft a Consumer Complaint before the District Consumer Disputes Redressal Commission under Section 35 of the Consumer Protection…), `medical-negligence-complaint-draft` (Draft a medical-negligence complaint before the appropriate Consumer Disputes Redressal Commission (District / State / NCDRC per the…), and 4 more\n- **Agents** (6): `drafter` (Third agent in the Indian consumer drafting pipeline), `format` (Second agent in the Indian consumer drafting pipeline), `overseer` (Sixth and final agent in the Indian consumer drafting pipeline), `reader` (First agent in the Indian consumer drafting pipeline), `refiner` (Fifth agent in the Indian consumer drafting pipeline), `verifier` (Fourth agent in the Indian consumer drafting pipeline)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install indian-consumer-drafting@claude-community` from `Wolfgangrush/indian-consumer-drafting`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot"
  ],
